    passageEn: 'At the blazing center of our Sun, temperatures exceed fifteen million degrees Celsius alongside incomprehensible gravitational pressures. Under these extreme conditions, hydrogen nuclei possess sufficient kinetic energy to overcome mutual electrostatic Coulomb repulsion. Through the proton-proton chain nuclear reaction, four hydrogen protons fuse to form a single stable helium nucleus. Because the final helium nucleus weighs slightly less than four loose protons, the missing mass converts into pure radiant energy according to Einstein\'s mass-energy equation E=mc². This perpetual thermonuclear furnace produces the vital warmth and sunlight that sustains terrestrial biology.',
